From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:17:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Split customer-facing site into a Render Static Site

The customer pages (home, products, gallery, quote) are now built into ./dist
and deployed as a Render Static Site, while the API, uploads and admin pages
stay on the existing Node web service. All functionality is preserved.

- add public/config.js: resolves the API origin at runtime, prefixes API and
  media URLs, and repoints admin links at the web service
- route all customer-facing fetches and image URLs through apiUrl()/mediaUrl()
- restrict CORS to an allowlist configured via STATIC_SITE_ORIGINS
- add build-static.sh and a two-service render.yaml blueprint

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
