Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add website publishing controls to the admin panel

Content edits (products, prices, gallery, business details) are served from
the API and are already live instantly. A static rebuild is only needed when
the page files themselves change, so this adds an explicit way to trigger one.

- publish.js: calls the static site's Render Deploy Hook, with debouncing so a
  burst of admin edits collapses into a single build
- GET/POST /api/admin/publish for status and manual publishing
- new "Website" tab in the admin panel with plain-language status and an
  "Update website now" button
- optional AUTO_PUBLISH=true rebuilds automatically after content changes
- render.yaml: autoDeploy on both services, plus the new env vars

